# Defect 2636, lane lane-include, 2026-11-21: a surface fixture rather than a
# `run` case, since every build of a `path` entry says so on stderr.
#
# A program holding by value the record of a `path` package's group whose
# header, `rec2636.h`, the package does not ship. With `--include` naming
# `inc/`, the folder that holds the library's header, both units read that
# one file, and the build runs; until the repair the file was refused
# `shadowed_header` as standing in for the package's own, which it never had.
# No mark: built plainly, no folder holds the header, and that refusal is
# `ffi_missing_header`'s.
use <rec>/rec

function main()
    p: rec.Pair = rec.make(a: 3, b: 4)
    print(rec.scaled(p))
